    "message": "Does not account for if someone submits a VirtualTool that happens to have a reference in it's inner tools equal to itself.   Effects all versions up to this verison. A fix is in effect for later versions and has a customizable limit for how deep to Look in a VirtualTool. \n-\nIf you *must* keep using this. Please note this is unsupported as of this time, and I would recommend to ensure your use of VirtualTools (aka tools that are defined via the ButlerSDK VirtualTool NuGet class) are trusted and ensure they are not broken (or malicious). \n\n-\nThe bug effects how the ToolSurfaceScope class maps declared attributes for requested permissions.",
    "reasons": [
      "Other",
      "Legacy",
      "CriticalBugs"
    ]
  },
